    "check": "returned unopposed: nine candidates nominated on Tuesday 7 August 1934 for the nine seats (Belfast Telegraph, image read; the same nine in the Frontier Sentinel); the same nine are the commissioners present at the first meeting, where Edward McGonigle was elected chairman and J. J. Fegan vice-chairman (Newry Reporter, 4 September 1934, p. 5)",
