  "note": "First election of Kilkeel Town Commissioners after the electors adopted the Towns Improvement (Ireland) Act, 1854, at a meeting of 14 May 1934, with nine commissioners directed (Newry Reporter, 19 June 1934, p. 5). A public meeting on Monday 30 July agreed a list to avoid a contest (Newry Reporter, 2 August 1934, p. 5); nine candidates were nominated on Tuesday 7 August 1934 for the nine seats, so there was no poll, and the round is filed on the nomination day. The new body first met on 31 August 1934. Returned unopposed. Names as printed in the nomination report; the first-meeting report spells Edward McGonigle, James J. Fegan, Robert J. Ferguson and Herbert H. Stevenson."
